WEBVTT

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:06.850
GIANT STEP

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.970
I'm the Basquasher, Dan JD!

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:13.980
Dan!

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.480
Hey, Dan!

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.070
Hey, I said, hey!

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:18.330
Man, shut up!

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:27.660
Hey, you Bigfoot there!

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.870
Put a lid on it or I'm gonna have to kick your ass!

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:32.930
There's only so much crap I can take, so...

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:33.710
Hey!

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:44.600
The hell?

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.030
The bastard jumped straight to basquatting...

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:51.240
Hey, this happened once before, right?

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.300
Bastard.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.950
He thinks it's all going his way.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:06.950
God dammit!

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.080
You! Bring it on!

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.310
Have you lost your mind?

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:11.960
Shut up!

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:13.620
We'll die!

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.460
We'll die, die, die!

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.970
I'll catch it if it's the last thing I do!

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:34.560
Gimme the best you got and I'll <i>take</i> it!

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:49.090
Say your prayers, pigs!

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:52.740
Get stinking drunk on the fleeting peace you'll get tonight!

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.320
Oh, Sela!

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.040
Gimme another beer!

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.190
Fried chicken for me!

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:00.550
Coming right up!

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:01.500
No problem!

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:10.750
No, wait!

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.000
No takebacks!

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:12.850
Aren't you a man?

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:19.520
And now, entertainment news.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:22.690
As the Basquash boom continues to gain popularity,

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:27.280
the town of Tetrapall on the outskirts of Side Candy has...

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.540
So what's getting you down? {sz: tc "tasogareteru" if possible, seems like some idiom}

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:37.990
Oh, Alan has more than I thought!

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.620
Stop that, please!

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.640
These might really develop into something!

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:43.980
{bg}Th-that spot...

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.630
Where?

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.090
Now it's my turn!

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:51.890
Let's go!

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.190
There you go.

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:04.400
Try all you want,

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.900
but basketball is the only way I fight.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.360
Come on. I'll let you play me.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.820
As you can see, {time this up through "goran no you ni"}

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:18.250
here at Mooneyes' Aries Hospital,

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:21.360
crowds of Eclipse fans have gathered day after day.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:24.860
Miss Sela, you are such a...

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:27.630
Well, it's just so cute when they fit in your hands!

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:30.850
Shh!

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:36.410
Their management has commented that for now,

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:42.020
Eclipse will take a break from appearances until Rouge's condition improves.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:47.050
However, because they have said nothing about the name or severity of the illness,

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:51.990
some sources speculate that her condition may be more serious than originally believed.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.550
Settle it, Dan!

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:11.260
Not a chance!

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:48.420
What kind of ball was that...?

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:50.250
I smell a tasty smell!

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:51.380
You think you can eat the ball?

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:55.170
I've never seen anything like that before!

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.670
You're not bad!

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:00.100
I'm Dan!

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.860
I'm Spanky!

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.120
Haven't seen that type of Bigfoot before either.

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.530
What model is that?

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:07.170
It's a fatso.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:10.250
If it doesn't go on a diet it might...

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.510
His face is huge!

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:17.770
Too big to eat.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:21.120
That's... <i>not</i> a Bigfoot?

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.450
I'm a person.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.100
Miyuki showed me a photo!

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.460
Are you from the moon?

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:30.610
Moon?

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:32.500
You've been to the moon?

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:35.840
Well, I wouldn't say we've really been there...

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.980
We circled it and got slapped down...

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:41.490
And when we crash-landed back on
 Earthdash we went in a little too deep.

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:43.220
'Cause he's an idiot.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:44.960
I see.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.710
I'm Naviga.

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:49.000
Naviga, huh?

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:52.370
Well, I guess I'll call you "Navi" from now on.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.770
Why leave off the "ga"?

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:58.100
Dan can't remember long names!

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.280
Shut up...

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:02.510
You're weird.

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.660
I'm not weird.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:08.970
Destroy!

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:19.930
Destroy!

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:45.540
Overdoing things, as always.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:50.350
Falcon!

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:51.880
Why are you here?

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:54.150
I heard a rumor that some guy who should've gone to the moon...

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:57.900
...was kicking up dust somewhere else completely.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:01.300
Saying, "Scream my name and spread the word."

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:06.850
Underground.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:09.980
So this is the town that stole your left arm and left leg.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:19.650
Kill him! Kill him! Kill him!

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:21.600
Iceman Hotty.

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:25.410
The man who tried to fight me with nothing but a ball.

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:28.580
That's quite unique.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:35.290
If you're going to bear a grudge, hate the legend, not me.

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:37.490
Legend?

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:41.380
The legend is what makes you a liability. {lit,. The legend is what means you must be erased.}

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:43.170
What are you talking about?!

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:52.600
Stop!

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:54.400
This is farewell.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:56.770
Bad luck for you, brokedown legend.

00:07:56.770 --> 00:08:00.570
No!!

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.870
Falcon, do you believe in the legend?

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:52.830
Legend?

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:54.460
I...

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:57.350
I have to find out.

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:00.470
I'm here, in this town, alive.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:03.180
What does that mean?

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:08.310
I wasn't chosen. I was thrown away like trash.

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:10.970
Why was I drawn back here where it all began?

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:15.020
Maybe it's because I ought to live in shame.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:18.520
That's philosophy.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.530
No, that's the legend.

00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:41.120
I have a new role for you two to play.

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:43.740
Everything is accelerating.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:46.300
It's nearly time for the curtain to rise on a legend.

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:49.860
Does that mean you have no further use for idols?

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:53.100
It's not hard to lead the masses by the nose.

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:56.720
That's...

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:00.380
"Debt King Dan JD Finally Leaves For Mooneyes."

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:02.800
"Rocket Malfunction For Dan's Team?"

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:05.740
"Wrong Orbit Drops Team Back to Earthdash"...

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:11.850
The man of legend will step offstage, and starting now all eyes will be on you.

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:14.700
As... Basquash players, you mean?

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:17.210
You object?

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:18.790
Hardly.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:20.760
Give us the job!

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.880
Once Rouge gets better, I'm sure she'll say the same thing!

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:28.400
Thank you, Violette, Citron.

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:48.780
"Man of Legend Spotted in Underground."

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:51.910
"What Will Happen to the Lunar League Season?" {sz: Referring to the Lunar League, which is missing Team Basquash.}

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:05.750
Hey.

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:09.630
Is it fun digging up rocks all day long?

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:11.910
Not rocks.

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:13.360
It's ultimite.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.560
What's that?

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.800
I don't really know.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:20.250
I don't know, but mining is my job.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:24.490
That totally does not inspire basquatting.

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:27.150
Hey, you gotta work if you want to eat!

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:28.190
You're one to talk.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.330
So Navi,

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.660
did I ever meet you a long time ago?

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:40.910
Nope. I'd remember that red hair.

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:42.710
Yeah...

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:45.190
If we met, it's not likely we'd forget...

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:46.600
Dunno.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:48.820
Dan's brain is special!

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:49.920
You be quiet.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:52.040
So Navi,

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:54.960
what do you say to getting out of here and playing Basquash with me?

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:56.390
Not an option.

00:11:56.390 --> 00:11:58.330
Why not?

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:01.570
You could play Basquash without even needing a Bigfoot!

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:04.780
From how you played before, that's what you really want, right?

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:08.420
Being stuck down here in a hole is a total waste!

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:15.110
Come with me.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:17.530
There's something I want to show you.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:23.210
That's a freakin' huge bounty!

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:26.590
If I brought in that head, I'd never have to work again!

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:28.150
They say he's in Dead Bottom!

00:12:28.150 --> 00:12:30.110
And Price already left!

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:32.260
What's all this?

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:34.540
Maybe they plan to start a war.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:37.680
Is there a kid named Miyuki here?

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:40.810
Could you deliver a message to Miyuki Ayukawa?

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:42.870
"Your big sister is here."

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:56.100
As I recall, you hate me.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.620
More precisely, I hate your grandfather.

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:04.010
You're an old acquaintance?

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.790
How nice of you to visit and say so.

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:08.200
No...

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:11.940
I want to meet the man of legend.

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:13.920
The... man of legend?

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:15.380
You mean Mr. Dan?

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:16.620
Yes.

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:19.710
Right now he's the most popular person in town.

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:28.030
What is this place?

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:29.720
Those are graves.

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:30.400
Graves?

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:36.300
Our ancestors were brought here from the moon to mine ultimite.

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:40.910
My friends who died on Earthdash sleep here.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.060
Ultimite is poisonous.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:47.110
We're resistant to that poison.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:50.090
That's why we were brought down here.

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:57.070
But over a few hundred years we started losing our resistance.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:01.350
Everyone else died one by one, and now I'm all that's left.

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:02.600
Does that mean...

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:05.780
I'm the last.

00:14:06.270 --> 00:14:10.410
So have to stay here and protect my friends' graves.

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:12.810
I can't go with you.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:15.270
What?

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:17.820
I don't get your reasoning at all.

00:14:23.030 --> 00:14:26.420
Is this river really the way to go?!

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:29.370
It is if you want to outrun the bounty hunters.

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:31.750
That way!

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:32.570
This way!

00:14:33.110 --> 00:14:34.000
Which way?

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:35.380
I don't know!

00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:41.410
This doesn't mean we trust you!

00:14:41.410 --> 00:14:43.700
If you trust, you can be betrayed.

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:45.770
I learned that from your grandfather.

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.090
Mr. Dan...

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:54.440
Someone's... calling?

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:56.250
Hark...

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:58.360
What is that sweet scent?

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:01.160
It smells delicious.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.390
Hey, Alan!

00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:05.160
Pay more attention to balancing!

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:06.160
Are you listening, Alan?!

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:06.910
I'll grope you again!

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:10.680
No, not that way!

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:14.220
No! That's even worse!

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:17.920
A tunnel!

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:22.310
I've seen that mech before...

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:26.920
So how does it feel having that for a teammate, Iceman?

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:31.230
It might surprise you, Falcon.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.540
Accepting each others' strengths and weaknesses...

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:37.170
That's what teammates do.

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:43.510
I don't know, but if Coco...

00:15:43.510 --> 00:15:45.380
That's Dan's little sister!

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:47.800
Yeah. If my sister...

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:50.000
She's cute and has her head on right

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.920
and I'm proud of her, but...

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:58.240
If I died and Coco left a flower on my grave every day,

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:00.800
I'd be happy. Of course I'd be happy.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:04.790
But if her life ended there,

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:06.680
I wouldn't be happy at all.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:08.360
I'd say so.

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:11.350
"You don't have to come any more."

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:14.290
"Go live your own life!"

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:18.630
"What were you born to do?"

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:24.500
The ball tells me how you feel.

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:29.870
Someone who's no Basquasher could never throw a ball like that!

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:36.850
Navi, you think your dead friends will like it if all you do is protect their graves?

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:41.790
If you make it out of here and play Basquash, they'll like that more!

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:44.940
I don't understand what you mean.

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:49.260
If you become a legend and make this place famous, that'd be enough!

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:51.910
Then your friends wouldn't be lonely.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.020
That's crazy.

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:57.410
Dan's always crazy.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:16:59.180
Friends, huh?

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:06.710
What is it, Dan?

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.150
Am I hearing things? {I'm guessing that's the spirit of the line}

00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:10.370
Just now I thought I heard Alan and the rest...

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:19.520
Y-You guys!

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:25.470
Mr. Dan!

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:27.260
Hey, just a—! Alan!

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:30.350
I'm so glad! We were worried!

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:35.020
A-And I, uh, they made me do really embarassing things...

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:36.960
Whatever, just let go!

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:38.060
Hi, honey.

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:41.100
Did you love me so much you followed even to the depths of the Earth?

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:42.940
Yes.

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:46.590
I thought I'd bury you so you could never crawl back up to daylight.

00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:49.580
Oh no!

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.690
Dan, whose Bigfoot is this?

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:55.030
Pleased to meet you.

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:57.950
I'm Naviga. Not a Bigfoot.

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:10.260
S-Sorry. I didn't mean to startle you.

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:14.390
Not a Bigfoot? Then what is he?

00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:15.550
A giant?

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:17.660
{hehe sound} Surprised?

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:20.340
He's one of the same guys who were on the moon!

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:22.150
His name's Navi!

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:25.400
No, it's Naviga, actually.

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:29.900
One of the legendary giants was on Earthdash...

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:31.100
A giant?

00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:32.720
You came from the moon?

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:34.130
Then...

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:41.020
It's like the town in the desert...

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:43.920
It's... calling me?

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:47.090
Are these your friends, Dan?

00:18:47.090 --> 00:18:48.080
Yeah!

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:49.850
We're all Basquashers!

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:51.090
Basquashers...

00:18:52.620 --> 00:18:55.310
Sorry I startled you. I—

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:01.610
Sorry.

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:03.270
Can we go yet?

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:09.120
So this is the man of legend.

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:11.140
Bit short, isn't he?

00:19:11.140 --> 00:19:13.000
Speak for yourself!

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:14.780
Who is this woman anyway?

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:16.510
Explanations later.

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:19.290
Pretty soon this won't be a place where we can stand and talk.

00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:21.750
Here comes another one!

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:25.590
One after another...

00:19:25.590 --> 00:19:27.780
Getting a lot of visitors today!

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:35.620
Oh, it's you!

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:36.890
Dan even managed to remember!

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:38.690
Oh, that's good!

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:40.890
So you got out of that cell too!

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:42.730
I'm glad!

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:45.980
That man will cut you down if you get too close, Dan JD.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:49.110
His name is the Price of Hell.

00:19:49.650 --> 00:19:52.160
He's the best bounty hunter in Underground.

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:54.000
Also known as the Legend Hunter.

00:19:54.620 --> 00:19:56.120
In other words, a paid killer.

00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:57.240
Killer?

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:06.130
It was him who made Iceman's body the way it is.

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:12.310
Is that so?

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:15.200
Thank you, Thousand.

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:18.490
Now I don't have to waste time introducing myself.

00:20:18.490 --> 00:20:20.180
Why the hell did you come here?

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.320
Why else?

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:28.320
A certain person paid for your death.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:32.600
If you're going to hold a grudge, Dan JD,

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:34.070
hate the legend, not me.

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:38.200
The legend is what makes you a liability.

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:40.250
Time to die...

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:42.250
...and take the legend with you!

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:54.630
Any man known as a legend...

00:20:54.630 --> 00:20:56.970
...must prevail over all that stands in his way.

00:20:56.970 --> 00:20:59.930
If he dies at my hands, then he wasn't the one!

00:20:59.930 --> 00:21:02.690
Next time, Memory of You.

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:06.650
NEXT TIME

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:01.890
MEMORY OF YOU

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:02.140
MEMORY OF YOU

00:21:02.180 --> 00:21:06.650
MEMORY OF YOU

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:05.280
Why not die and be just a memory?
